    {
      "body": "@merrymercy @hnyls2002 small robustness fix in the tokenizer manager: the count-based admission caps can't tell a 4k prompt from a 500k one, so a long-context burst over-commits prefill memory and OOM-crashes the server. --max-inflight-prefill-tokens bounds the in-flight prompt tokens and rejects up front instead. On GLM-5.2-FP8 an 8x500k burst went from taking the whole server down to clean rejects, and it's default-unset so it's a no-op unless set. Could one of you kick CI with /tag-and-rerun-ci and take a look?",
